    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493310117/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Yesterday I began to read Ricci’s “Pintoricchio” for review. Bernhard is soaking himself in Franciscan literature. I called on the Chapmans (out), and Gertrude, and on Mr. Cannon; and in the morning we called on the Duse’s and had little chat with her nice daughter.
Today I called on Mrs. Ross, who came back with me. Mr. Lestrange came, and Mr. Cannon with Mrs. Volmer. Then came the Duse, her daughter and the daughter’s friend - both of them studying to be nurses. The Duse was very gracious to Mr. Cannon, and when he went she was  fascinating . We spoke of Maeterlinck’s “Monna Vanna” and the way his wife acts if, and then, to our surprise, """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 188 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

